  "answer": "I'll add an optional manufacturer website that is stored, accepted on create/update, returned in manufacturer JSON, and rejected unless it starts with http:// or https://. First I'll read the project skill and locate the manufacturer model and REST API.The manufacturer JSON is built in a few places, so the website has to be stored on the entity and copied through both the create/update path and every response that includes a manufacturer. Invalid URLs will be rejected before anything is saved.Manufacturers now have an optional `website` URL. It is stored on the `MANUFACTURER` table, accepted on the private create and update APIs, and returned as `website` on the manufacturer detail and list responses and on the manufacturer nested in a product. A value that does not start with `http://` or `https://` is rejected with HTTP 400 before anything is saved. A blank website is still allowed.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core-model,sm-shop-model,sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 on an invalid website\", \"website persisted and returned on manufacturer detail, list, and product JSON\"], \"missing\": [\"an integration test or documented request sequence for manufacturer create, update, list, and product manufacturer JSON\"]}",
